  "semantic_slots": {
    "objects": "Actual A_N=Fin N→Bool, actual normalized count μ_N, true sign±1, S_N=(sqrt N)^-1 sum signs, actual pushforward probability laws; literal gaussianReal0,1 target. Standardized RGO rho/r is ultimate separate context.",
    "domains": "Every natural N including0; successor n+1 positive for variance-one normalization. Finite discrete canonical carrier, real output/Borel weak topology, real/complex Bochner integrals genuinely finite internally.",
    "quantifiers": "One actual family of laws for all N, exact map equality for all N, law0=dirac0, successor weak convergence; no random iid law, actual map identity, mean/second moment or limit supplied by a caller.",
    "assumptions": "Scalar actual-count background is unconditional apart from canonical typing. Source potential/eta assumptions stay on future SPHMC consumer; single balanced-law probability/L1/mean0/moment1 and adapters are internal obligations.",
    "conclusion": "Only actual law family and weak gaussianReal0,1 convergence; no entropy/energy/LSI/T2/W2/main/cost output.",
    "scopes": "External SLT real product has NeZero N and no Boolean-count/N0 result. Direct finite-count factorization and finite real-product transport are authored alternatives. Infinite-iid route has genuine construction/prefix-law gaps. Existing compiled Mathlib scalar leaf is not ASTIS producer.",
    "constant_dependencies": "Actual mass2^-N, normalization1/sqrt N, variance1 Gaussian. N0 second moment0. Future full-flip factor4 and finite half-to-Gaussian2 energy transfer are external residuals, not consequences of weak CLT."
